{
  "id": "urn:visionflow:page:policy-decision-point",
  "title": "Policy Decision Point",
  "slug": "policy-decision-point",
  "public": true,
  "classIri": "urn:ngm:class:policy-decision-point",
  "domain": "security",
  "definition": "A Policy Decision Point (PDP) is the logical component in an attribute-based or policy-based access control architecture that evaluates access requests against a set of authorisation policies and returns a permit, deny, or indeterminate decision. The PDP receives a request context\u2014including subject attributes, resource attributes, action, and environment conditions\u2014from a Policy Enforcement Point (PEP), retrieves applicable policies from a Policy Information Point (PIP) or Policy Administration Point (PAP), and applies the XACML combining algorithms or equivalent logic to reach a binding decision. PDPs are the computational core of fine-grained, dynamic authorisation systems used in zero-trust security architectures, identity federation, API gateways, and cloud IAM platforms.",
